    "body": "RFC 5545:\n\n> A.1.  New Restrictions\n> [...]\n> [4]  The value type of the \"DTEND\" or \"DUE\" properties MUST match the value type of \"DTSTART\" property.\n\nThis appears to already be covered by the following passage in HTML5:\n\n> If the property with the name `dtend` is present within an item with the type http://microformats.org/profile/hcalendar#vevent that has a property with the name `dtstart` whose value is a _valid date string_, then the value of the property with the name `dtend` must be text that is a _valid date string_ also. Otherwise, the value of the property must be text that is a _valid global date and time string_.\n\n(HTML5 doesn't seem to include DUE.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/167378729/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
