    "body": "RFC 5545:\n\n> A.1.  New Restrictions\n> [...]\n> [3]  The BYHOUR, BYMINUTE, and BYSECOND rule parts MUST NOT be  specified in the \"RRULE\" property when the \"DTSTART\" property is specified as a DATE value.\n\nHTML doesn't mention any of `BYHOUR`, `BYMINUTE`, or `BYSECOND`.\nThis presumably only affects HTML indirectly, by constraining the valid values of `rrule`, which is already delegated to the iCalendar spec.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
