    "body": "RFC 5545:\n\n> A.2.  Restrictions Removed\n> 1.  The \"DTSTART\" and \"DTEND\" properties are no longer required to be specified as date with local time and time zone reference when used with a recurrence rule.\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/microdata.html#conversion-to-icalendar:md-vevent-dtstart is stricter than this. I would guess that HTML is already intentionally simplifying here and wouldn't want to apply this loosening. That algorithm section doesn't cite iCalendar anyway.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
